Z||000000||BlackStang95||12-01-2001||09:19 PM||||Those who bought your cars new and still have and drive them...what originally attracted you to the car?  Did you know all about how good they handle and how the fires were fixed or were you looking for a different looking commuter and were pleasently surprised?  Bring on the stories  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||Springtyme||12-01-2001||10:23 PM||||To *try* to keep this clean I'm gonna be the first response. I'm not the original owner, but don't flame me. I'm the second owner, the first owner got it from her husband in '88 as an anniversary present. He bought it brand new for her. She didn't like driving it much because it was so small, but she did like the way it handeled.<BR>Anyway, her husband died earlier this year of cancer and she wanted to drive his car since it was bigger and more reliable for the long trip to Chicago where her daughter and her daughters baby live. Thats where I came in and took it off her hands   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>For those of you who don't know, yes I'm crazy.<BR>~~~~~<BR>1988 Coupe 4 cyl.<BR>0-infinity in 2 seconds<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Springtyme_1.JPG"> <p>[This message has been edited by Springtyme (edited 12-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fformula88||12-02-2001||12:33 AM||||I was a long way from being able to drive in 1988, so I am obviously not the original owner either.  However, I can answer your questions.  I was attracted to the Fiero because my father had owned one for years!  It was an 87 coupe (4 cyl) and I had driven it a lot after I got my license.  Whatr I liked most about it was that it was unique in a few different ways.  It had a plastic body (which in Buffalo is a very good thing!  No rust).  It was a two seater sports car, and it was unique and not like anything else on the road.  I think its uniqueness was my favorite attribute.  That 87 was not fast, and on the economy 195/75R14's it certainly weasn't carving too many corners, and yet it was an absolute blast to drive!  I simply fell in love with it and had to have my own!<P>Originally, I think the uniqeness of the cars design... plastic body, mid-engine, combined with its attractive price tag brought buyers into the showroom!  It may have been billed as a "commuter", but back in the day there weren't many sports cars that could be bought that had the style, performance and price tag of a Fiero.  Against cars from its era, it may not always have been the best in every area of performance but it was competitive and its styling was ahead of the competition (MR2 was much boxier when rounded was coming in style, and the CRX was fairly plain). ||||reg||1
Z||000003||SLYGUY||12-02-2001||01:30 AM||||In '88 I was only 16. I could drive yes, but finance a new Fiero,no. Always liked them though. I remember seeing so many of the 84-86s running around town back then. Not as much now. <P>My parents bought a 87 wingless medium red GT in 1990 and the next year traded it in on a bright red 88 Duke. I fell in love with the car then and did what most people seem to do and got married and had 2 kids. Well, the kids are still here!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I bought my first Fiero in 1992. It was an 86 SEV6. Red with silver two tone. Loved that car. Momentary loss of consciousness resulted in trading it in on a 4x4. <P>2 months ago I got my 88GT. Loved it at first sight and it has been a great little car.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Sly<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ViewImage.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||LoW_KeY||12-02-2001||09:54 AM||||Well like a lot of people I got one when I was 16 84 black coupe auto for 1000 bucks with 54,000 miles.  I enjoyed the car a lot and rode in many other cars, but I just didn't enjoy the drive.<P>Rode in my friends 87 GT and all the memorys of the V6 came back (from a previous test drive my dad and I went on) and that's when I knew I wanted a V6.  I wanted a GT but it didn't happen, I'm not sad about it no because I ran across the formula and about died I was like ooooh yeah!<P>It needed some work, but I got it all done and to this day everyone stares and looks.  I guess I like the whole mid-engine, how it handles, looks, unique, and how the car is a mystery to everyone who doesn't own one.  They always say death trap and keep ramblin' on but hey I let them you can't change ignorant people, but it cracks me up how they think they know everything about it when they've never even drove one  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Now I just need to find something this fun to drive in the winter time  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>-KC<P>------------------<BR>AIM: FierFormula88   <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kcbanner.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000005||Raydar||12-02-2001||10:15 AM||||My first Fiero was an 85 GT that I bought new. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero1_6.jpg"> <BR>What attracted me to it was the Indy pace car styling and the V-6 rumble and power. Was nearly as quick as a lot of V-8 cars of the same era. (But not the 350 Monza in the carport.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> )<BR>Also, I had just finished rebuilding a 70 Cutlass that my (then) G/F had wrecked. Fought with rust every step of the way. Plastic body panels seemed like a *very* good idea.<BR>Traded it in 88 because I just *had* to have a new Firebird Formula. And two more seats.<BR>Got my 88 coupe in December of 97, and my Formula in April of this year.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fierochic88||12-02-2001||10:48 AM||||Double post - sorry<BR>Jennifer<p>[This message has been edited by Fierochic88 (edited 12-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fierochic88||12-02-2001||10:48 AM||||Well my dad actually won his 1985 GT and has had it ever since!  Right now it has somewhere around 60,000 miles on it.  It is still in great shape!  He always liked Fieros but with a new family it wasn't a practical car.  So instead, he got one for free!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  We've had it ever since and love the car to death!  <P>Jennifer<P>------------------<BR>IM Username:  FieroChic88<BR>Silver 1988 GT<BR>Silver 1986 2m4<BR>Cobalt Blue 85 GT<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.personal.psu.edu/users/j/j/jjr161/Fierochic88Signature.jpg"> ||||reg||1
